            <ArticleTitle>Imaging abnormalities that correlate with joint pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>289-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bjsm.2010.081398</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article summarises evidence on structural pathology in the joint that causes joint pain. Evidence, mostly from studies using MRI scans in persons with and without joint pain has suggested that pain often originates in bone or synovium.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
